        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SessionStateMachine/Lane_Human",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ActivityLog/Lane_Operator",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_FeatureStaging/Lane_Human",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeManagerWatch/Lane_Owner",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeToMain/Lane_Owner",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeTrain/Lane_Owner",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SaturationMetaMerge/Lane_Owner",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_StalledAgentTriage/Lane_User"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ContentAcquisition/Lane_Person",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_ContentAcquisition",
      "label": "Contributor",
      "scopeNote": "Both of this lane's tasks are optional by design, not merely possible: P_Respond's 'or neither' is a real, accepted outcome rather than a stall, and A_Ask already states what happens if nothing comes back — so this lane can contribute nothing at all and the process still proceeds, which is not true of the sign-off lanes elsewhere in this corpus.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CopyOutMaterialized/Lane_Reader",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CopyOutMaterialized",
      "label": "Reader (any actor)",
      "scopeNote": "ANY reader, not only an editor. Refusing a copy would not protect the original, because the original is protected by being read-only; a permission here would only stop people working. So this lane has no entry condition, and the one decision in it is about the TARGET rather than about the actor.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Ingestion/Lane_0",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_Ingestion",
      "label": "Contributor (human or agent)",
      "scopeNote": "Whoever puts the file in the queue.\n\n\"HUMAN OR AGENT\" IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A HEDGE: both place files here. That is why Task_Place is a plain `bpmn:task` rather than a `userTask` — asserting a human performs it would contradict the lane's own role graph, which is what `activity-fulfilment-kind` exists to catch.\n\nWHAT THE LANE IS ACCOUNTABLE FOR, and where it ends. Choosing a route, writing the bytes into the DECLARED queue of the layer that will own them, and discharging afterwards whatever that route could not — the web form has no working tree, so no pre-commit hook and no generator runs on it. The lane does NOT ingest and does not clean the queue: it hands over, and Lane_1 takes it from there. `upload-routes` carries the routes and their obligations.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MaterializeRemote/Lane_0",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MaterializeRemote",
      "label": "Contributor (human or agent)",
      "scopeNote": "One task, asked first for a reason: working vs. archival is not just an input to the five gates that follow, it changes what three of them MEAN — an archival copy is the only one that can discharge source loss, and a process that gated before asking this would be judging a copy against obligations it did not yet know applied.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/materialize-remote.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MethodologyFromSource/Lane_Owner",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MethodologyFromSource",
      "label": "Owner",
      "scopeNote": "Shares the source and the intent in chat, answers the coordination question, and decides the adoption. Only the owner accepts an adoption or moves a proposal's status.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/methodology-from-source.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation/Lane_ML_Owner",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation",
      "label": "Owner",
      "scopeNote": "Decides which layers and locales are translated, and when locale PRs may be merged. The merge window set here binds the lead's merge step and the refresh watcher alike. Official sign-off is also this person's, and is a separate process.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/multi-locale-translation.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RefreshMaterialized/Lane_0",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_RefreshMaterialized",
      "label": "Contributor (human or agent)",
      "scopeNote": "Reached only when both upstream and local changed, which is the one case this process refuses to resolve by rule: which side wins depends on why the local edit was made, a fact only this lane has.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/refresh-materialized.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SampleImport/Lane_0",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SampleImport",
      "label": "Contributor (human or agent)",
      "scopeNote": "One decision, and it is the one no file answers: what the sample is FOR. Which items, into which store, and whether the result is meant to last. The last question decides the destination, and asking it after the copy exists would mean moving a copy that was already landed somewhere under the wrong obligations.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/sample-import.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SubscribeKg/Lane_0",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SubscribeKg",
      "label": "Subscriber (the folio's owner)",
      "scopeNote": "Every CHOICE in the walk is made here and nowhere else: which substrate and at which commit, which of its subgraphs, asset classes and harnesses to hold. The engine never chooses a part on the subscriber's behalf — a subgraph not chosen stays referenced, which is a state, not an omission — and the pre-check on harness needs sends the choice back here rather than resolving it silently.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/subscribe-kg.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RelatedWork/Lane_User",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_RelatedWork",
      "label": "User",
      "scopeNote": "Answers one question: coordinate or not, and how. The question arrives with its context, options and a recommendation, so it can be answered without opening anything (interaction-modality §4.1).",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/related-work.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SecureAgentPermissions/Lane_Owner",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SecureAgentPermissions",
      "label": "Owner",
      "scopeNote": "Grants, narrows or refuses each permission, having been told what it allows and why. The only lane that can grant.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/secure-agent-permissions.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SessionStateMachine/Lane_Human",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SessionStateMachine",
      "label": "Human actor",
      "scopeNote": "Entered only when Gateway_ActorKnown cannot confirm an actor — the one fact in this whole record that the machine cannot recover by reading the repository — and answered once: the response is recorded so this lane is never re-entered for the same session, which is what keeps asking who is acting from becoming a repeated interruption.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ActivityLog/Lane_Operator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_ActivityLog",
      "label": "Log operator (human)",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane in this diagram that chooses: one entry by id, or everything. It was split out from a single conflated lane because a person's choice and a scheduled sweep's fixed program are not the same actor, which is why the sweep below has a lane of its own rather than sharing this one.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_FeatureStaging/Lane_Human",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_FeatureStaging",
      "label": "Human actor",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane whose actor cannot be a machine — `deletion-requires-confirmation` is not satisfied by a click, so H_Confirm must repeat the slug rather than approve generically, which is what stops a confirmation from an earlier run being replayed against a different preview. It precedes Start_Dispatch rather than following it, so the dispatch entry point cannot fire at all until this lane has acted.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeManagerWatch/Lane_Owner",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeManagerWatch",
      "label": "Owner",
      "scopeNote": "Approves in the merge manager's session only, one card per batch. An approval given in a sibling's session does not authorise a merge.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeToMain/Lane_Owner",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeToMain",
      "label": "Owner",
      "scopeNote": "The repository owner. The only lane that can say `merge`. Answers a question that carried the evidence; a person, never an agent, a sibling session or a bot.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-to-main.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeTrain/Lane_Owner",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeTrain",
      "label": "Owner",
      "scopeNote": "May override a placement, always with a reason. Releasing a merge to `main` is no longer drawn here: it is the Owner lane of `merge-to-main.bpmn`, which `Call_MergeToMain` descends into, so the owner's release has one definition for every process that merges rather than one per diagram.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-train.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SaturationMetaMerge/Lane_Owner",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/user",
