      "label": "Copier's own folio/",
      "scopeNote": "Where the copy lands: the copier's own folio, never a scratch area, because a directory nobody declared is a directory nobody gates. The two writes here are ordered and both required — Task_Land puts the bytes somewhere, Task_RecordProvenance says what they are a copy OF, and a process that stopped after the first would produce a file indistinguishable from original work one rename later.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/copy-out-materialized.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CopyIntoFolio/Lane_Author",
