      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_HumanTranslation",
      "label": "Subject-Matter Expert / Reviewer",
      "scopeNote": "The one reviewer lane in this corpus where sign-off is acceptance: Task_Signoff makes the translation official directly, with no separate editor lane after it, because translation fidelity is the acceptance criterion and there is no different judgement left for an editor to add.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/human-translation-workflow.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Review/Lane_Reviewer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/reviewer",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_Review",
      "label": "Reviewer / SME",
      "scopeNote": "Makes exactly one decision on its own — what changed, at Task_ClassifyChange — and for everything after that descends into a subprocess, taking on the narrative- or code-reviewer role for that call path only rather than carrying both statically. A change that is both prose and code goes to the pair review; neither role widens the other.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/content/review-task.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_HarnessRendering/Lane_Reviewer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/reviewer",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_HarnessRendering",
      "label": "Reviewer",
      "scopeNote": "The person reading the harness. Reading needs nothing; writing needs a write tool and the permission to use it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/harness-default-rendering.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ThemeUIReview/Lane_Reviewer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/reviewer",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_ThemeUIReview",
      "label": "Reviewer",
      "scopeNote": "The single point in this process where a person looks rather than a tool measures, reached only after all four agent passes are done — so what this lane judges is the ingested assets as a whole, in the design they are for — not any one axis in isolation. Its finding is the only thing that can send the process to A_RaiseFindings; a clean ingest, a passing accessibility check and a correct branding pass can each be true and still miss what only laying the assets out and looking catches.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_NarrativeCodeReview/Lane_PairReviewer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/reviewer",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_NarrativeCodeReview",
      "label": "Reviewer",
      "scopeNote": "The generic reviewer, taking this lane for the call path only: it reads what the pair checks left open and settles each item one of three ways. It can attest and raise findings but cannot overrule a checker on its own say-so — that is what the call into adjudication is for.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/narrative-code-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamAdoption/Lane_Review",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/reviewer",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_UpstreamAdoption",
      "label": "Reviewer / SME",
      "scopeNote": "Narrower than a general release review: the question is only whether what upstream-pins.json lists as bound still holds against the deployed MVP, not whether the new version is good on its own terms, and a finding here (GW_Findings) sends the run back to the Agent lane's own impact analysis rather than stopping it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/upstream-version-adoption.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/review-coordinator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Review coordinator",
      "title": "Review coordinator",
      "notation": "review-coordinator",
      "definition": "Organises a review without deciding it. Pulls tagged review comments in, splits a large change into slices by section, assigns each slice to a reviewer of the right role, and watches coverage until every changed block has a verdict or a reasoned waiver. Cannot accept or reject: that is the editor's lane, and the separation is the owner's ruling (2026-09-23, bean en2d). Not a reviewer: it does not inherit one, because assigning a slice is not reading it.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/narrative-reviewer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Narrative reviewer",
      "title": "Narrative reviewer",
      "notation": "narrative-reviewer",
      "definition": "Judges PROSE — register and voice, the editorial dependencies a reader needs, and translation. Entered by DESCENDING into Process_NarrativeReview: the actor keeps its outer review role and adds these skills along that call path, rather than every reviewer carrying them everywhere.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_NarrativeReview/Lane_NarrativeReviewer",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_VoiceReview/Lane_NarrativeReviewer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_NarrativeReview/Lane_NarrativeReviewer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/narrative-reviewer",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_NarrativeReview",
      "label": "Narrative reviewer",
      "scopeNote": "Turns mechanical matches into verdicts, not the other way round: `qa-checkers-voice.ts`, `qa-checkers-uses.ts` and `translation-block-qa.ts` produce candidates, and this lane is the only place a phrase-list hit becomes a wrong-register finding, an out-of-genre criterion, a stated exception, or nothing at all. House voice is adjudicated before any activated overlay is even reached, because an overlay adds to the house judgement rather than replacing it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/content/review-narrative.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_VoiceReview/Lane_NarrativeReviewer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/narrative-reviewer",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_VoiceReview",
      "label": "Narrative reviewer",
      "scopeNote": "Runs every active voice to completion rather than stopping at the first, because rules from separate voices are UNIONED rather than merged — two voices can both flag capitalisation and both findings must stand, so folding voice N+1's pass into voice N's would lose which voice raised what. At each citation, this lane also has to route the defect to the right place: a rule its own citation does not support goes to Task_RuleIsWrong as a finding against the VOICE, never into Task_Adjudicate, which only ever judges the block.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/content/voice-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/code-reviewer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Code reviewer",
      "title": "Code reviewer",
      "notation": "code-reviewer",
      "definition": "Judges the knowledge graph's CODE nodes — Tool definitions in the `tools` graph and schema definition nodes under `schemas/`. Not ordinary code review: the question is whether the NODE is sound — does it declare what it is, do its references resolve, is the mechanism it advertises the one that runs — which a passing test suite does not answer. Entered by DESCENDING into Process_CodeReview.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CodeReview/Lane_CodeReviewer",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CodeChangeReview/Lane_Reviewer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CodeReview/Lane_CodeReviewer",
