        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Deliver/Lane_BA",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Needs/Lane_BA",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Requirements/Lane_BA",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM/Lane_BA",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Signoff/Lane_BA",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_OptionsAnalysis/Lane_BusinessAnalyst",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SwotAnalysis/Lane_BusinessAnalyst",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RequirementsFiling/Lane_BA"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Close/Lane_BA",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Close",
      "label": "BA / Feature Requestor",
      "scopeNote": "Stands between stakeholder sign-off and the agent's close as an independent check against defined criteria — decision-audit, not a re-ask of the same yes/no the stakeholders already gave — and A_Close's own documentation says it is reachable ONLY through this confirmation, so the agent has no path to closing that bypasses it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_DataModel/Lane_BA",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_DataModel",
      "label": "BA / Feature Requestor",
      "scopeNote": "Confirms naming only — are these the entities meant — and stops there: Lane_Stakeholders asks the separate, operational question about cardinality next, and the two are kept apart on purpose, because collapsing them into one review is how a wrong cardinality ships invisibly.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-data-model.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Deliver/Lane_BA",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Deliver",
      "label": "BA / Feature Requestor",
      "scopeNote": "Every signal that can send the loop back to A_Implement is filtered through this lane first: BA_ReviewIncrement judges behaviour rather than code, GW_MVPReady decides whether accumulated increments are worth showing stakeholders at all, and BA_TranslateFeedback is the only step that turns S_TestMVP's raw findings into direction the agent can act on. Nothing stakeholder-facing reaches Lane_Agent without passing through here.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-deliver.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Needs/Lane_BA",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Needs",
      "label": "BA / Feature Requestor",
      "scopeNote": "The single review here is what GW_Needs is literally named for — \"BA approves?\" — even though Lane_Stakeholders' confirmation sits between this task and that gateway in the flow; the phase's own documentation makes clear the loop needs both, so reading the gate label alone would miss half of what it takes to exit it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-needs.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Requirements/Lane_BA",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Requirements",
      "label": "BA / Feature Requestor",
      "scopeNote": "The one checkpoint between the agent's comparison and the stakeholders' sign-off: BA_ReviewReqs is where someone who can read the impact analysis on its own technical terms vouches for it, because Lane_Stakeholders reviews only at defined checkpoints and needs the requirement already in a form they can approve without re-deriving it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM/Lane_BA",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM",
      "label": "BA / Feature Requestor",
      "scopeNote": "The one activity in this diagram that is not a subprocess call: states the capability gap in its own words and, per its own documentation, does not need to know any of what follows is called CRDM. The six phases translate the need into that vocabulary, not the other way round.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Signoff/Lane_BA",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Signoff",
      "label": "BA / Feature Requestor",
      "scopeNote": "Makes two decisions of different character here: BA_Signoff approves what was drafted, and BA_ChooseKg commits it — or explicitly does not — to a knowledge-graph destination, where NONE is a legitimate answer rather than a refusal to answer. Only this lane may decide that a requirement is fully carried by the code and becomes a commit and nothing else; an agent that decided so on its own would be placing a node in somebody else's graph.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-signoff.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_OptionsAnalysis/Lane_BusinessAnalyst",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_OptionsAnalysis",
      "label": "Business analyst",
      "scopeNote": "This lane's deliverable is the recommendation together with the rejected options — a rejected option with no record is a dead end the next agent walks back into — but it never authorises anything; A_Record hands both to whoever called the subprocess, and the decision stays theirs. Answering GW_Trigger `no` is not a skipped step either: End_TriggerNotMet is recorded as a distinct outcome from a completed comparison, because a caller unable to tell \"not needed\" from \"we chose X\" cannot audit either one.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/options-analysis.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SwotAnalysis/Lane_BusinessAnalyst",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SwotAnalysis",
      "label": "Business analyst",
      "scopeNote": "Performs the scan and the crossing. This lane owns the analysis and owns nothing else: it does not authorise, and it does not choose between options. Its deliverable is four lists, the four matched strategies, and an explicit record of what could not be classified.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/swot-analysis.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RequirementsFiling/Lane_BA",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/business-analyst",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_RequirementsFiling",
      "label": "BA / Feature Requestor",
      "scopeNote": "Reviews the filed requirement's normative statements, three-axis traceability links, concern-group placement in docs/requirements/index.md, and any supersession or retirement transition, issuing the human adjudication required before a RequirementSet reaches accepted.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/requirements-filing.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/terminologist",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Terminologist",
      "title": "Terminologist",
      "notation": "terminologist",
      "definition": "Owns coded concepts and value sets — the vocabulary a DAK is expressed in.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translation-coordinator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Translation coordinator",
      "title": "Translation coordinator",
      "notation": "translation-coordinator",
      "definition": "Decides what is translated, into which languages, and when a translation is accepted.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Translation Coordinator"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_HumanTranslation/Lane_Coordinator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_HumanTranslation/Lane_Coordinator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translation-coordinator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_HumanTranslation",
      "label": "Translation Coordinator",
      "scopeNote": "Owns the completeness gate, Gateway_Complete, a different question from the accuracy Lane_Reviewer judges later: this lane can send work back to the translator for missing or fuzzy strings before a single sentence has been checked for meaning.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/human-translation-workflow.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Human translator",
      "title": "Human translator",
      "notation": "translator",
      "definition": "Produces the target-language text. Distinct from the coordinator because accepting one's own translation is the gate this separation removes.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Human Translator"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_HumanTranslation/Lane_Translator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_HumanTranslation/Lane_Translator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_HumanTranslation",
      "label": "Human Translator",
      "scopeNote": "Task_TranslateInTool is where both loops in this process land — an incompleteness request from the coordinator and a correction from the reviewer — so nothing in the task itself says which one sent the work back; only the annotations that travel with each loop carry that distinction.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/human-translation-workflow.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translation-adjudicator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Translation adjudicator",
      "title": "Translation adjudicator",
      "notation": "translation-adjudicator",
      "definition": "Adjudicator who settles a disagreement between machine and human translation. The first specialisation of `adjudicator`, and the only one that existed before the role did — its lane documentation in translation-workflow.bpmn is where \"a reviewer reports, an adjudicator settles\" was written down.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Human reviewer / adjudicator"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Translation/Lane_Reviewer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Translation/Lane_Reviewer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translation-adjudicator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_Translation",
      "label": "Human reviewer / adjudicator",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane here that JUDGES. Mechanical translation QA produces candidates — a flagged passage, a terminology miss, a staleness verdict — and a candidate is not a finding until somebody decides it is. This lane is where that decision is made, and it is the lane that signs the translation off, because the actor who resolves a disputed passage is the one who can say the whole is fit to publish.\n\nAdjudicator rather than reviewer alone, and the distinction is the accountability: a reviewer reports, an adjudicator settles. The word is used here because the passage reaching this lane is one where a checker and a translator disagree, and somebody has to choose between them WITH a reason. That reason is the record, not the choice.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/translation-workflow.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translation-source-lead",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Source-language lead",
      "title": "Source-language lead",
      "notation": "translation-source-lead",
      "definition": "Owns the source-language side of a translation into several locales: extracts every template once, in one shared source PR merged to main before any locale starts, validates each locale PR and merges it inside the owner's merge window, files the one issue for source-text errors the translators report, and keeps the refresh watcher that brings every locale up to date when the source moves. Distinct from `translation-coordinator`, who decides what is translated and accepts it: this position does the source-side work, and an agent can do it.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Source-language lead (watcher)",
        "Translators"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation/Lane_ML_Lead",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRefresh/Lane_TR_Lead",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_WebAppPublish/Lane_Translators"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation/Lane_ML_Lead",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translation-source-lead",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation",
      "label": "Source-language lead",
      "scopeNote": "The one party that touches the source. It extracts every template once, merges that source PR first, collects source-text errors into one issue, validates and merges each locale PR inside the owner's window, and keeps the watcher that runs `translation-refresh`.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/multi-locale-translation.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRefresh/Lane_TR_Lead",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translation-source-lead",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TranslationRefresh",
      "label": "Source-language lead (watcher)",
      "scopeNote": "Owns the watcher. It decides whether anything changed from the files, not from memory, refreshes the templates once for every locale, and merges the layer's PR only where the layer declares merge-when-green, every check is green and the round trip records no fail.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/translation-refresh.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_WebAppPublish/Lane_Translators",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/translation-source-lead",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_WebAppPublish",
      "label": "Translators",
      "scopeNote": "The source-language lead and the locale translators of the harness's translation process. The app's strings are one more template to them.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/web-app-publish.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/locale-translator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Locale translator",
      "title": "Locale translator",
      "notation": "locale-translator",
      "definition": "Produces one locale's catalogues from the shared templates: the `.po` files, their unofficial translation-node manifests and the locale's terminology supplement, then the gates, the QA report and the locale PR. Never re-extracts and never edits the source; a source-text error is reported, not fixed in the translation. One lane covers every locale, each run once per locale. Distinct from `translator`, a person working in their own tool under human-translation-workflow: this position may be an agent, and what it produces is unofficial until a person signs it off.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Locale translator (one per locale)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation/Lane_ML_Translator",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRefresh/Lane_TR_Translator",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRoundTrip/Lane_RT_Translator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation/Lane_ML_Translator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/locale-translator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MultiLocaleTranslation",
      "label": "Locale translator (one per locale)",
      "scopeNote": "One lane for every locale: each step here runs once per locale, in parallel, and each locale's work is its own branch and its own PR. A translator starts from the merged templates, never from its own extraction, and reports a source error rather than translating around it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/multi-locale-translation.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRefresh/Lane_TR_Translator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/locale-translator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TranslationRefresh",
      "label": "Locale translator",
      "scopeNote": "The same position as in the first translation, now working on a delta: only the strings the merge left empty or fuzzy, in every locale, then the gates and the round trip over those strings.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/translation-refresh.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRoundTrip/Lane_RT_Translator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/locale-translator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TranslationRoundTrip",
      "label": "Locale translator",
      "scopeNote": "The producer. It chooses what is checked, by a rule stated before any result is seen, and hands on the target strings alone. It may record one thing here, \"could not dispatch\", because without that state a producer forbidden from writing a verdict has nothing honest to write.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/translation-round-trip.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/back-translator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Back-translator",
      "title": "Back-translator",
      "notation": "back-translator",
      "definition": "The checker of a translation round trip: renders a sample of the target-language text back into the source language from the target text alone, with no tools and without seeing the source. It rules on nothing. Its rendering is the intermediate the adjudicator reads (`untainted-verification`, rule 1: neither party sees what would let it shortcut).",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRoundTrip/Lane_RT_Back"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRoundTrip/Lane_RT_Back",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/back-translator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TranslationRoundTrip",
      "label": "Back-translator",
      "scopeNote": "Sees the target strings and nothing else: not the source, not the repository, no tools. Shown the source, it writes the source back and the check passes without measuring anything.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/translation-round-trip.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/round-trip-adjudicator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Round-trip adjudicator",
      "title": "Round-trip adjudicator",
      "notation": "round-trip-adjudicator",
      "definition": "Rules on a translation round trip: given the source strings and the back-translation, and never the target text, it pre-screens every pair mechanically, reads each flagged pair in full, and records drift or not-drift for each with the reason. A specialisation of `adjudicator` for the translation instance of untainted verification; it adds the translation-specific drift definition.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRoundTrip/Lane_RT_Adjudicator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TranslationRoundTrip/Lane_RT_Adjudicator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/round-trip-adjudicator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TranslationRoundTrip",
      "label": "Round-trip adjudicator",
      "scopeNote": "Sees the source strings and the back-translation, never the target text, and rules each pair drift or not drift with its reason. Both halves of the drift definition are in front of it, so that inflection and word order are not ruled as drift.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/translation-round-trip.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/adjudicator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Adjudicator",
      "title": "Adjudicator",
      "notation": "adjudicator",
      "definition": "Settles a criterion whose reviewer entries disagree, and records WHY. Inherits `reviewer` because an adjudicator is a reviewer with one added entitlement — the `adjudication` permission — and the separation is the point: a reviewer reports, an adjudicator settles, and a process where every reviewer could settle has no way to say who decided. The KNOWLEDGE spreads (several roles carry the `adjudication` skill, because each has to tell an adjudicable disagreement from a complaint); the ENTITLEMENT does not, and lives on the actor as a permission.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Adjudication/Lane_Adjudicator",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CriterionAdjudication/Lane_CriterionAdjudicator",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_WireframeDesignReview/Lane_Adjudicator"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Adjudication/Lane_Adjudicator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/adjudicator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_Adjudication",
      "label": "Adjudicator",
      "scopeNote": "Every decision and every write is here, and that concentration is the accountability: a reviewer reports, an adjudicator settles, and a process where the settling were spread across lanes would have no way to say who decided. The role admits person and agent — `refresh-materialized` already states the reason, \"a human or agentic decision, never a merge rule\" — and the judgement steps are drawn as plain tasks rather than user tasks so the diagram does not assert a person where an agent is legitimate.\n\nA_Dispatch is in this lane although the adjudicator is its SUBJECT rather than its performer, and that is deliberate: whoever composes the brief chooses what the adjudicator may see, so putting it anywhere else would let the composing party grade its own input. `untainted-verification` states the rule the step enforces — the adjudicator is given the checker's output and never the artefact.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/adjudication.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CriterionAdjudication/Lane_CriterionAdjudicator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/adjudicator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CriterionAdjudication",
      "label": "Adjudicator",
      "scopeNote": "One lane, because every step here is the adjudicator's: asking the question, choosing among the answers, and writing the entry. The feedback provider's lane is in `adjudication.bpmn`, where stating a finding happens — a provider has no entitlement to settle what it reported, and drawing it here would suggest otherwise.\n\nThe role admits person and agent. `refresh-materialized` already gives the reason in its own words — \"a human or agentic decision, never a merge rule\" — and the steps are plain tasks rather than user tasks so the diagram does not assert a person where an agent is legitimate.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/criterion-adjudication.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_WireframeDesignReview/Lane_Adjudicator",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/adjudicator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_WireframeDesignReview",
      "label": "Adjudicator",
      "scopeNote": "Reached only when entries for one criterion disagree. Settles the disagreement with a reason, and decides between surviving candidates through options analysis.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/wireframe-design-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/feedback-provider",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Feedback provider",
      "title": "Feedback provider",
      "notation": "feedback-provider",
      "definition": "Offers a finding on content or code — a script checker, a review agent, a reader, an SME. PLURAL by design: an adjudication is the judgement of one or more feedback providers' feedback, and the process draws the lane once for any number of them. Not an adjudicator: this role states what it found and on what evidence, and has no entitlement to settle the disagreement its finding creates.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Feedback providers"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Adjudication/Lane_FeedbackProvider",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_WireframeDesignReview/Lane_Reviewers"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Adjudication/Lane_FeedbackProvider",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/feedback-provider",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_Adjudication",
      "label": "Feedback provider",
      "scopeNote": "Drawn once for any number of providers — the owner's \"Judgment of &gt;= 1 Feedback Provider's feedback\" — because the process does not change with the count and a lane per provider would say it did. A script checker, a review agent, a reader and an SME all act here, which is why the role admits person, agent and system alike.\n\nThis lane knows the one thing the lane below does not: WHAT IT ACTUALLY LOOKED AT. A_StateFinding exists to move that across, and without it the adjudicator cannot tell a real disagreement from two parties reading different things — which looks identical from the sidecar and is not the same defect at all. The lane holds no gateway and reaches no end event on purpose: a provider states a finding and has no entitlement to settle it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/adjudication.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_WireframeDesignReview/Lane_Reviewers",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/feedback-provider",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_WireframeDesignReview",
      "label": "Feedback providers",
      "scopeNote": "One or more reviewers (agent and human) who see candidates shuffled, without their author, and record pass, warn or fail per criterion with a reason. There are no scores and no averages.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/wireframe-design-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/stakeholder",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Stakeholder",
      "title": "Stakeholder",
      "notation": "stakeholder",
      "definition": "Signs off that a requirement is met. Carries no skills deliberately: sign-off is a judgement, not a procedure, and a skill here would suggest an agent could supply it.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Stakeholders"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Close/Lane_Stakeholders",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_DataModel/Lane_Stakeholders",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Deliver/Lane_Stakeholders",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Needs/Lane_Stakeholders",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Requirements/Lane_Stakeholders",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SwotAnalysis/Lane_Stakeholder"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Close/Lane_Stakeholders",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/stakeholder",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Close",
      "label": "Stakeholders",
      "scopeNote": "The first of three sequential checks this diagram exists to enforce in order — sign off, confirm, close, never any other sequence — and what is being signed off here is the delivered FEATURE on the issue, not the requirement model that crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn's Lane_Stakeholders approved earlier in the process.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_DataModel/Lane_Stakeholders",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/stakeholder",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_DataModel",
      "label": "Stakeholders",
      "scopeNote": "Answers the operational half the BA cannot — not what a thing is but how many of it there really is — because that is knowable only to the people who run the process day to day. It is also the step this process's STRICT policy exists for: skipped under time pressure, a model looks finished without it, which is exactly how a hole where the exceptions live would ship unnoticed.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-data-model.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Deliver/Lane_Stakeholders",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/stakeholder",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Deliver",
      "label": "Stakeholders",
      "scopeNote": "Tests in the stakeholder's own workflow and data rather than against the acceptance criteria BA_ReviewIncrement already checked — a second, independent pass rather than a repeat of the first. GW_StakeholderOK's `findings` branch does not hand the agent anything directly; it hands raw results to BA_TranslateFeedback, which is this lane's boundary: it reports what works and what does not, and translating that into direction is somebody else's lane.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-deliver.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Needs/Lane_Stakeholders",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/stakeholder",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Needs",
      "label": "Stakeholders",
      "scopeNote": "The task itself carries no documentation of its own, so this lane's entry is the only place recording what \"confirm\" means in Phase 1: recognising the synthesised needs statement as actually theirs, immediately before the loop gate — not, as in the later data-model phase, judging a cardinality, because there is no model yet to have one.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-needs.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Requirements/Lane_Stakeholders",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/stakeholder",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Requirements",
      "label": "Stakeholders",
      "scopeNote": "The verdict GW_Reqs reads to decide between ending the phase and sending A_DefineReqs around again — a narrower approval than crdm-close.bpmn's final feature sign-off, since what is being approved here is the REQUIREMENT model itself, not that the delivered feature satisfies it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SwotAnalysis/Lane_Stakeholder",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/stakeholder",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SwotAnalysis",
      "label": "Stakeholder",
      "scopeNote": "Consulted, in a lane of their own because the source names group discussion as a property of the method rather than as good practice around it: SWOT \"promotes group discussion about strategic issues\" and pools knowledge through participatory techniques. It is also the mitigation for the limitation the source states most sharply — that a list of strengths is \"bound up with aspirations, biases, and hope of the individuals involved\". A single analyst producing four lists alone has performed the technique's shape without the part that checks it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/swot-analysis.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Authoring agent",
      "title": "Authoring agent",
      "notation": "authoring-agent",
      "definition": "The session agent doing the work. The broadest skill set here, and the one whose membership most needs auditing.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Agent",
        "Agent (playing the machine)",
        "Agent (this session)",
