      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "Briefs, measures the signals, runs declare-detangle-isolate, reports what would move, seeds the repositories once they exist, and adopts each later release. Verification is always by re-running a gate, never by a change looking right.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/kg/kg-separation.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SubKgLifecycle/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SubKgLifecycle",
      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "Declares the sub-KG in place and grows it, reports what would move before each irreversible step, drains the open pull requests that keep the source from settling, and copies the staged contents into the new repository with their history.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/kg/sub-kg-lifecycle.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_AskThePerson/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_AskThePerson",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Composes, writes and offers the question, then acts on the answer or the default. Never treats a dismissed card as a choice. The person's answer step is drawn in bootstrap's discussion, in its Requestor lane: Answers with one tap. Typing is never required: the person this was written for has very limited hand function.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/ask-the-person.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Close/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Close",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Holds no judgement in this diagram: both prior lanes already decided — sign-off, then confirmation against criteria — so this lane's only accountability is executing the close exactly when authorised and never before, on an issue that is the stakeholder's record rather than the agent's to close on its own reading of the thread.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-close.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_DataModel/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_DataModel",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Does the actual modelling — entities, relations, and the declaration that makes the model machine-readable rather than prose — and absorbs the entire cost of a revise: the gate loops back to A_Entities whichever confirmation failed, BA's or the stakeholders', so this lane cannot assume a cardinality objection leaves its entities untouched.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-data-model.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Deliver/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Deliver",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Every loop-back in this phase — a rejected increment, an MVP not ready, stakeholder feedback — lands on A_Implement rather than on Call_OptionsAnalysis, so this lane always reworks an approach already chosen and never re-selects one. Deciding that the APPROACH itself is wrong is not this lane's call: that belongs to the calling step in crdm-requirements.bpmn, one level up.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-deliver.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Issue/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Issue",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "The only CRDM sub-diagram in this slice where the BA has no lane of its own: A_AskCreate is still an Agent-lane activity, so the permission this process exists to enforce is obtained out of band rather than modelled as a cross-lane handoff, unlike crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn and crdm-close.bpmn elsewhere in the same methodology.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-issue-linking.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Needs/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Needs",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Drafts the needs statement but never decides it is right — A_Synthesise is the sole target when GW_Needs loops back — and this process's own documentation calls an unconfirmed synthesis \"an agent's summary, not a requirement,\" which is exactly what this lane alone produces before the two lanes below it look at it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-needs.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Requirements/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Requirements",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Owns Phases 2 through 4a end to end, but the revise loop (GW_Reqs' 'revise' branch) re-enters at A_DefineReqs rather than back at A_MapWorkflow — so mapping the current workflow is this lane's one-time fact-finding, done once per phase run, while defining requirements and comparing options is what gets redone against BA feedback until Lane_Stakeholders approves. When a requirement changes a rendered surface, this lane also designs it before anything is built: GW_RenderedSurface sends it to Call_Wireframe, where the agent is the Designer of Process_WireframeDesignReview and posts its candidates for the BA to choose from. The call sits here rather than in Lane_BA because drawing and checking the candidates is the agent's work; the BA's part is the choice, made at BA_ReviewReqs.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-requirements-definition.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Holds the one gate whose \"no\" branch ends the entire process rather than routing into a child — GW_Feature's own documentation: a subprocess would have to re-ask the same question to route on the answer. From there it carries the BA's need through all six phases as a straight chain of subprocess calls, with no branching of its own.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-requirements.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CRDM_Signoff/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CRDM_Signoff",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Turns Lane_BA's two decisions into durable artefacts: A_CreateBeans and A_RecordKg each mint their own bean directly with the CLI, since the engine's own vocabulary has no create, only claim, note and resolve on an instance's bean. A_AnnounceBranch then closes the phase on its one path to End with no loop of its own, so it fires exactly once — Phase 6's own loops re-enter implementation on the same branch without ever crossing back through this edge.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/crdm-signoff.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RelatedWork/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_RelatedWork",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Searches, sorts and summarizes, and recommends. It never links, blocks, merges or comments on another piece of work before the user has answered, because coordinating is a commitment on behalf of the work's owners.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/related-work.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SecureAgentPermissions/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SecureAgentPermissions",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Finds out which agent Tool is acting, what the harness's processes need it to be allowed to do, and what is already granted; explains each missing permission; records and applies what the owner granted. Grants nothing to itself.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/secure-agent-permissions.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SessionStateMachine/Lane_Machine",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SessionStateMachine",
      "label": "Agent (playing the machine)",
      "scopeNote": "Classifies every turn into exactly one of three effects at Gateway_TurnEffect — nothing changed, state changed, ending — a fresh judgement each time because a table cannot key on intent and a wrong read is corrected by the next turn. It records that a bean was claimed or an instance closed, at A_UpdateSession, but performs none of those actions itself: the record and the thing it describes are kept deliberately separate.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/session-state-machine.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_WireframeDesignReview/Lane_Designer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_WireframeDesignReview",
      "label": "Designer",
      "scopeNote": "Writes the intent, produces candidates with real content, and runs the mechanical checks. Does not review its own candidates.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/wireframe-design-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ActivityLog/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_ActivityLog",
      "label": "Agent (this session)",
      "scopeNote": "Brackets its own work with a start and an end entry rather than leaving either implied, and reads Gateway_Capture rather than assuming it: persisting when capture is on, but merely reporting the setting — never silently dropping the entry — when it is off or could not be determined.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/activity-log.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_BeanClose/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_BeanClose",
      "label": "Agent (this session)",
      "scopeNote": "Closes only the bean its caller opened and claimed — Process_BeanOpen already sent someone else's to its sibling — and picks one of three recorded endings for it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/bean-close.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_BeanDrain/Lane_Drainer",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_BeanDrain",
      "label": "Drainer",
      "scopeNote": "Takes beans from its own list one at a time and runs each through OPEN, the work and CLOSE before it takes the next. Its only bean writes are the ones OPEN and CLOSE make; a bean OPEN finds is someone else's is marked skip on the queue and left alone. It asks for a refill rather than picking from another owner's list.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/bean-drain.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_BeanLifecycle/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_BeanLifecycle",
      "label": "Agent (this session)",
      "scopeNote": "Owns every transition on a bean it holds. Whether the bean is its own at all is decided inside Process_BeanOpen, whose sibling lane takes someone else's bean; this lane only reads the answer at GW_Yours and stops when it is not.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/bean-lifecycle.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_BeanOpen/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_BeanOpen",
      "label": "Agent (this session)",
      "scopeNote": "Checks, creates and claims a bean it may hold. Open_Owner is the one branch this lane cannot finish itself: a bean that turns out to be someone else's goes to Lane_Sibling, and nothing on it is resolved, scrapped or edited from here.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/bean-open.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CodeChangeReview/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CodeChangeReview",
      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "The `no-clean-run-over-an-empty-set` convention is bound at this lane specifically because this is the one lane that writes checks — Lane_Pipeline runs them and Lane_Reviewer reads someone else's, so a check with nothing to assert over is this lane's failure mode to guard against, nobody else's. Every activity that is not mechanical execution (Lane_Pipeline) or an outside judgement (Lane_Reviewer) sits here, including both loop-backs — a red gate returns to Task_Implement through Task_Diagnose, and review findings return to it through Task_AddressReview — so this lane never hands work off without also owning what comes back.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/code-change-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeBase/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeBase",
      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "Reached only when the command refused: an authored conflict, an undeclared path, or a resolution the gates could not reproduce. The refused paths are listed for it; what to do with an authored conflict is judgement.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeRefusal/Lane_Dispatched",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeRefusal",
      "label": "Dispatched agent",
      "scopeNote": "ONE agent with a modest budget, reached only when no live owner can be. May do what a declared pattern would have done; may NOT decide an authored conflict, which goes to the owner as a question.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RequirementsFiling/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_RequirementsFiling",
      "label": "Authoring Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Executes the deterministic filing steps under methodologies/requirements-filing-and-organisation.md: classifies the filing mode and concern group, promotes the proposal via git mv (preserving git blame and proposedIn), binds Requirement front matter and three-axis lineage, updates superseded or retired records in place, updates docs/requirements/index.md, runs check:requirements, and records the human sign-off attestation.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/requirements-filing.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SmeTestDataReview/Lane_Prepare",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SmeTestDataReview",
      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "Prepares the review package from the fixed test data set (`test-data-fixed/1.0.0`): either a worked case with system output for decision support, or a cohort with computed and expected values for an indicator definition.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/sme-test-data-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_StalledAgentTriage/Lane_Triage",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_StalledAgentTriage",
      "label": "Triage agent",
      "scopeNote": "Reads the footprint the stalled agents left, collects or reconstructs a handover report per agent, groups the work into 2-4 themes, and recommends. It never finishes, closes or deletes another agent's work.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestDataCuration/Lane_Author",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TestDataCuration",
      "label": "Authoring agent",
      "scopeNote": "Authors or curates the test data set: classifies whether the case requires a fixed curated set or a deterministic generated recipe, invokes the content-type specialisation subprocess on the generated branch or SME review on the fixed branch, and writes the self-identifying node into its declared graph directory.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamPinWatch/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_UpstreamPinWatch",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Entered only once Lane_Ci has confirmed a pin is behind and filed the issue, never to make that determination itself: A_PickUp's claim is what stops two sessions adopting the same bump. The judgement of adoption is not drawn here either — Call_Adopt hands it to its own reusable process, so this lane is only the hand-off from mechanical detection to judgement, not the judgement itself.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamAdoption/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_UpstreamAdoption",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Owns the whole MVP loop end to end except the two calls it cannot make: SF_UA_8 re-enters this lane's own A_Impact on a fixable finding rather than escalating, so a defect gets fixed and re-evidenced here before anyone outside the lane sees it, and Call_OptionsAnalysis sits here specifically because framing the options is not deciding among them — that judgement belongs to PM_Decide in a different lane entirely.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/upstream-version-adoption.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Ingestion engine",
      "title": "Ingestion engine",
      "notation": "ingestion-agent",
      "definition": "Runs unattended over a source corpus. No user is in the room, so every gate it reaches must be decidable from the material.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Agent",
        "Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)",
        "Ingestion engine (agent, runs unattended)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ContentAcquisition/Lane_Agent",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Ingestion/Lane_1",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MaterializeRemote/Lane_1",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RefreshMaterialized/Lane_1",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SampleImport/Lane_1",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SubscribeKg/Lane_1",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_IngestTheme/Lane_0",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ThemeUIReview/Lane_Agent"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ContentAcquisition/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_ContentAcquisition",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "This lane is not unattended, unlike the same role elsewhere: A_Ask and A_Route both wait on Lane_Person, for minutes or days, because there is no material yet to make a gate decidable from — that only becomes true once a file or description exists. Acquisition ends at the moment something lands in the queue; everything past that boundary is document-ingestion.bpmn's actually-unattended run, not this one.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/content-acquisition.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_Ingestion/Lane_1",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_Ingestion",
      "label": "Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)",
      "scopeNote": "Runs the basic flow from the metadata step to the placement in library/, unattended: every decision in it is decidable from the material and its declarations. It asks one question — is the asset materialized? — and that is answered from the materialization state vocabulary (`schemas/kg/materialization-state.ts`), not by judgement. It does NOT choose a reader for the bytes, derive sections or blocks, or describe images: those are a refining process's work, which calls this flow first.\n\nTHE FLOW ENDS IN THIS LANE. The asset catalogued in library/ — held, or recorded as referenced — is the terminal state, and every knowledge-graph reference to it resolves through library/ from here; a refining process continues from it rather than being drawn into this one. There is no separate corpus lane: it would hold only the end event, and a lane with no activity has no performer to describe.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/document-ingestion.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MaterializeRemote/Lane_1",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MaterializeRemote",
      "label": "Ingestion engine (agent, runs unattended)",
      "scopeNote": "Runs the five gates in a fixed order and reaches Task_Fetch only after Gateway_Gates finds none of them refused. Before the first gate it resolves the request against the source DESCRIPTOR (Task_Enumerate), because the size being gated is the closure's, not the request's — size, restrictions, copyright, retention, source loss — so this lane's job is not one decision but five independent ones, each of which can send the process to Task_StayRef on its own. It does not get to average them: `unknown` on any single gate is enough to keep the node `referenced` rather than `materialized`.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/materialize-remote.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RefreshMaterialized/Lane_1",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_RefreshMaterialized",
      "label": "Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)",
      "scopeNote": "Runs whichever of the two paths Gateway_Purpose selects. On the working path it answers the two comparisons — upstream and local — whose combination Gateway_Both reads to decide whether a human must adjudicate; on the archival path it never compares to the source at all, since fixity asks only whether the copy itself rotted.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/refresh-materialized.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SampleImport/Lane_1",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SampleImport",
      "label": "Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)",
      "scopeNote": "Calls the two shared subprocesses and does the part that is this process's own: landing the copy in the destination the contributor chose, importing it into the store, and testing the import. It never re-asks a gate: it acts on materialize-remote's outcome. It also answers the second entry, an upstream change to a permanent sample, by calling refresh-materialized rather than re-importing.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/sample-import.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SubscribeKg/Lane_1",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SubscribeKg",
      "label": "Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)",
      "scopeNote": "Validates the substrate at the pin, then walks the chosen parts one at a time: each subgraph or asset through the shared materialisation subprocess, each held copy through the shared refresh, each harness by writing its config. Every loop here re-enters its decision after each part, so a refusal on one part is recorded and the walk continues to the next rather than aborting the subscription.",
      "source": "cat-harness/library/processes/subscribe-kg.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_IngestTheme/Lane_0",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_IngestTheme",
      "label": "Ingestion Engine (agent, runs unattended)",
      "scopeNote": "Every step in this diagram is this lane's, and each treats the source as evidence to be recorded rather than resolved: contradictions in the source are kept as data rather than silently picked, values the source is silent on are marked as a choice rather than dressed up as a measurement, and a missing layout ends in refusal rather than a theme quietly degraded to the ones that were supplied.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/ingest-theme.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_ThemeUIReview/Lane_Agent",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ingestion-agent",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_ThemeUIReview",
      "label": "Agent",
      "scopeNote": "Four measured passes into R_Judge — inventory, accessibility, branding, locales — each one required to MEASURE rather than assert, because an automated pass alone misses defects a rendered look catches. If GW_Findings comes back yes, this lane still does not fix anything: A_RaiseFindings sends the finding back to whoever authored the theme choice, since picking it was a judgement call this lane does not get to override.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/ui/theme-ui-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
