      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeRequest/Lane_Sibling",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/sibling-session",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeRequest",
      "label": "Sibling session",
      "scopeNote": "Any coding agent with a PR ready to merge. It first checks whether a merge manager is active; if none is and one is needed, it elects one with its siblings by the fixed rule; a lone or lapsed session manages its own PRs. It never merges another session's PR, never pushes to another session's branch, and treats a merge manager that does not acknowledge within the stall window as stalled. It never waits for a dependency to merge: it stacks on the dependency PR and keeps working.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-request.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeTrain/Lane_Sibling",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/sibling-session",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeTrain",
      "label": "Sibling session",
      "scopeNote": "The session that owns a handed-back PR. Fixes it on its own branch and re-signals ready; never merged on its behalf.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-train.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SaturationMetaMerge/Lane_Sibling",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/sibling-session",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SaturationMetaMerge",
      "label": "Sibling session",
      "scopeNote": "Every other session with a PR in the queue. It acts once: it stops pushing when the hold arrives and names the head it wants merged, so the steward stacks a branch nobody is still moving. It does not choose what lands; the owner does.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/merge-steward",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Merge steward",
      "title": "Merge steward",
      "notation": "merge-steward",
      "definition": "Stewards writes to ONE watched ref -- a long-lived branch several processes write and something downstream consumes serially. The ref is a parameter of the LANE INSTANCE, not of this persona, so `main`, `gh-pages` and each `cat/cat-harness/*` store branch can each have a steward without a schema change; a ref qualifies when a declaring directory's `storage` (or `source`) names it, or it is `main`/`gh-pages`. On `main` that work is a merge train: composes it from the queue, attributes and ejects on red, lands at the tested SHA. On a route-keyed ref it is coalescing: batches the writes arriving in one window into a single write. Decides nothing the reprioritisation table or the owner has not -- placement is computed by merge-priority.dmn, and landing waits for the owner's release, given in the steward's own session as one card per batch. Records decisions on queue entries and windows, never the host's facts. On `main` the lane is conditional: it is held while two or more active sessions have ready PRs in the same repositories and their merges slow each other down (contended runners, or PRs that conflict with or supersede each other), and lapses when that stops. With none active the sibling sessions elect one by a fixed rule (the owner of the P0 PR, else the earliest-created active session); a lone session is its own steward. The holder acknowledges each merge request within a heartbeat window, and a holder that stalls is replaced by re-election without it (owner rulings, 2026-11-07; skill merge-manager-watcher).",
      "altLabel": [
        "Merging session"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeManagerWatch/Lane_Steward",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeToMain/Lane_Merger",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeTrain/Lane_Steward",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SaturationMetaMerge/Lane_Steward"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeManagerWatch/Lane_Steward",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/merge-steward",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeManagerWatch",
      "label": "Merge steward",
      "scopeNote": "The merge manager: the one session holding the merge-steward lane, by the owner's word, by election, or for its own PRs only. Each wake it reads the open PRs, the runner queue, main's verdict and who owns each PR, acknowledges requests within the heartbeat, then routes to the process the queue needs or stays idle. It hands over explicitly when it stops; like any agent it may stall, and the siblings then re-elect.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-manager-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeToMain/Lane_Merger",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/merge-steward",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeToMain",
      "label": "Merging session",
      "scopeNote": "The merge steward while a Merge Manager is active; with none active, the PR's own session takes this lane (owner ruling 2026-10-06). Reads evidence, finds and records authorisation, merges and follows through. Never authorises: that is the owner's lane, and no reading of an instruction moves it here.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-to-main.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeTrain/Lane_Steward",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/merge-steward",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeTrain",
      "label": "Merge steward",
      "scopeNote": "Composes the train from the queue, decides nothing the placement table or the owner has not, attributes and ejects on red, and lands at the tested SHA.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-train.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SaturationMetaMerge/Lane_Steward",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/merge-steward",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SaturationMetaMerge",
      "label": "Merge steward",
      "scopeNote": "The merge manager, acting as merge steward for the duration of the drain. It notices the runners are saturated, holds the swarm, dry-runs the meta-merge and asks the owner with every PR named; on a yes it cancels the queued PR runs, builds and lands the meta-merge branch, releases the hold and reports. It never lands anything the owner's card did not name.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Build pipeline",
      "title": "Build pipeline",
      "notation": "build-pipeline",
      "definition": "Validates, renders and publishes, and watches whether that actually worked. A system lane: it runs a fixed program and exercises no judgement, so anything needing a decision belongs in a different lane. It carries `todo-manager` for the two CI-watcher dispatch points in `content-change-review`, which `claim` and `note` a bean and never `resolve` one -- claim is idempotent and note appends, both fixed programs, while deciding that a publish SUCCEEDED is the judgement this lane must not make (bean xom7: docs-site.yml failed 30 times while reporting its own exit code).",
      "altLabel": [
        "Automated Pipeline",
        "CI/CD Pipeline",
        "CI/CD pipeline",
        "Graph audit (system)",
        "Scheduled log sweep",
        "Universal Query Engine Runtime",
        "merge:main command"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
