      "label": "CI/CD pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Exists as a separate lane for one reason: what it tests — the merge of head into base — is not a claim the Agent lane could make about its own tree, so GW_CIGreen has to be fed by an independent run rather than by the agent reporting its own gates as done.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/code-change-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_CodeQualityGates/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_CodeQualityGates",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Joins every job before asking anything, then GW_Hard asks specifically about the HARD gates — the two warn-only results reach the same join but never the gate, so this lane's merge/block call is deliberately blind to a red warn-only step it also ran. No count is given here on purpose: this paragraph carried \"seven jobs, five hard\" and then \"six-and-four\", and each was wrong the next time a job was split or folded (beans `om30`, `7fu5`). Count the `# bpmn-node:` lines in the workflow instead.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/code-quality-gates.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_DocsSite/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_DocsSite",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "GitHub Actions runs every step; no step waits on a human decision.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/docs-site-publish.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_FeatureStaging/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_FeatureStaging",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Runs all three entry points — stage, cleanup, cleanup-dispatch — as one actor because none of the work in any of them needs judgement; the one step that does, confirming a dispatch deletion, was carved out into Lane_Human rather than left here. Every path that changes `branches/` writes its render-log entry in the SAME commit as the change, because a log push that can fail on its own is exactly how a preview vanishes with nothing on the branch saying why.\n\nA FOURTH trigger starts none of them, and that is deliberate rather than an omission from this diagram. `merge_group` is declared on the workflow so it REPORTS in the merge queue — a required check that never reports on a `merge_group` event leaves every queued pull request pending forever — and all three jobs skip on it. A preview exists for the reviewers of a pull request; a queue entry has none and lives for minutes. Without the skip, `stage`'s existing guards all pass on a queue run (`github.event.action` is empty and the event is not a dispatch), so it would publish `branches/&lt;slug&gt;/` named after the ephemeral `gh-readonly-queue/...` ref, and nothing would ever remove it — `Start_Closed` below fires on `pull_request_target: closed`, and a queue branch is never a pull request that closes. That is the `plj1` shape arriving once per MERGE rather than once per pull request.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/feature-staging.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_GeneratedFileDrift/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_GeneratedFileDrift",
      "label": "Build pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane: one mechanical step whose diff the gateway reads directly. There is no reviewer to hand off to; the check either matches or it does not.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/generated-file-drift.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_JsonLdDrift/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_JsonLdDrift",
      "label": "Build pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane: the job runs one shared check.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/jsonld-drift-check.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeBase/Lane_Command",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeBase",
      "label": "merge:main command",
      "scopeNote": "Mechanical. Decides nothing a declaration has not decided: a path no pattern names is refused, and the gate set, not this lane, judges the result.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-base.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeToMain/Lane_Pipeline",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeToMain",
      "label": "Build pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "CI, not an agent. Regenerates the harness projections of the knowledge graph on the PR head and commits them to the PR branch, so the head whose evidence is read next is the head that would land. Judges nothing.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-to-main.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeTrain/Lane_Pipeline",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeTrain",
      "label": "Build pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Mechanical: merges, regenerates and runs the gates, and reports. Judges nothing a declaration has not decided.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-train.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_PrChecksPresent/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_PrChecksPresent",
      "label": "Scheduled log sweep",
      "scopeNote": "Three exit states, and the job's own colour tracks none of them the way a reader would expect: a finding is fully recorded — issue tracked, PR commented — and the job still ends GREEN, because the finding is the repository's problem to see in the tracking issue, not this lane's to fail on. Only UNKNOWN turns the job itself RED, and one unreadable PR is enough to fail the whole sweep — this lane never reports a partial clean.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/pr-checks-present.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_PublishAlert/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_PublishAlert",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "The build pipeline, running unattended between the export and the deploy. Raises the one alert, the same way whichever step failed.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/publish-alert.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_PublishVerification/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_PublishVerification",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Runs every verifier over the exported documents before anything is deployed, and reports pass, fail or could-not-tell. It decides nothing about the release: the caller blocks on anything but a pass.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/publish-verification.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_QaPublish/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_QaPublish",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Runs both paths as fixed programs. It decides nothing that needs judgement: whether a token can write is read from the event, whether a push was accepted is the push's exit code (never its stderr — spike `3ds9` measured a harmless \"push negotiation failed; proceeding anyway\"), and what retention removes is `planPrune`'s rule. A PR whose state cannot be read is KEPT: could-not-determine never deletes.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/qa-publish.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_RepoHealth/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_RepoHealth",
      "label": "Scheduled log sweep",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane in this diagram, and everything it does is either checking or recording — never removing, which is deletion-requires-confirmation applied to the shape most tempted to break it. It is also where the inversion lives: a real finding leaves the job GREEN and speaks through one tracking issue edited in place, while \"could not tell\" is the only outcome that turns the job RED and leaves that issue deliberately untouched.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/repository-health-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SaturationMetaMerge/Lane_Pipeline",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SaturationMetaMerge",
      "label": "Build pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "The CI system, which runs main's checks once on the merged result. Its verdict is what the steward reports; it is drawn as its own lane because it is a system acting on a fixed program, not a choice anybody makes.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/saturation-meta-merge.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TrackedWatch/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TrackedWatch",
      "label": "Scheduled log sweep",
      "scopeNote": "Every path through it writes something: the tracking label, and the issue itself (opened, edited or closed). Keeping all of it in one lane is what makes 'one tracking issue, edited in place' enforceable.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/tracked-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamPinWatch/Lane_Ci",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/build-pipeline",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_UpstreamPinWatch",
      "label": "CI/CD Pipeline",
      "scopeNote": "Owns exactly three outcomes and must keep them visibly different: current closes the tracking issue, behind opens or edits it, and UNKNOWN leaves the issue untouched while failing the job anyway — a watchdog that goes blind must never read as clean, so this lane is the one place that distinction cannot be collapsed into a single pass or fail. It hands off at the first sign of judgement: the moment a bump needs adopting, that is Lane_Agent's, never this one's.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/upstream-pin-watch.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_UpstreamAdoption/Lane_Build",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
