      "label": "Portal (external consumer)",
      "scopeNote": "The only lane outside this layer's control, so P_Verify checks against an external trust anchor — the GDHCN trustlist — rather than against anything the pipeline itself asserts. When that trustlist cannot be reached, this lane's answer is `unknown`, and GW_Verified routes it the same way as a mismatch: to the last good version, never to a guessed pass.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/kg/kg-to-portal.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/log",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Activity log",
      "title": "Activity log",
      "notation": "log",
      "definition": "The agent activity log. A MECHANICAL role: it is written to at task start and task end, and emptied by an actor — one entry, all of them, or on a periodic sweep — and it decides nothing. Modelled on `work-plan` and `corpus`, the two existing stores; its skill is the contract it is held to. Its entries are held in the layer's unpublished store and never reach a published graph; the `activity-log` skill names the location, which is deliberately not repeated here because a role description IS published.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/session-record",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Session record",
      "title": "Session record",
      "notation": "session-record",
      "definition": "A session's context — who is acting, which instances are open, what it waits on. A MECHANICAL role: written to as the session moves and read by a sibling deciding whether a claim is live, and it decides nothing. Modelled on `work-plan`, `corpus` and `log`, the other stores. It carries `session-context` because the shape of what is written IS the discipline here — unlike `work-plan`, whose store has a CLI, this one is written by a machine that may be an LLM playing the part, so the schema is the contract.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
