      "label": "Discussion agent",
      "scopeNote": "The agent the person is talking with right now. Shows the hand-back, asks, marks every copy answered and routes the answer back.",
      "source": "cat-harness/processes/process/hand-back-to-discussion.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_BeanDrain/Lane_QueueKeeper",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/session-coordinator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_BeanDrain",
      "label": "Queue keeper",
      "scopeNote": "Holds the queue file and nothing else: builds it from every bean copy, grouped by owner with what was left out and why, and refills a drainer whose list runs dry. It never claims — a queue entry says who should take a bean, and only the drainer's OPEN says who did. One agent can hold this lane and the drainer lane at once.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/bean-drain.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_MergeRefusal/Lane_Steward",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/session-coordinator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_MergeRefusal",
      "label": "Merge steward",
      "scopeNote": "Coordinator and verifier of the hand-back: records, hands back, takes back when the fail condition fires, and closes. Never edits the bean's instructions after the executor claims it; later facts go to the PR.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/merge-refusal.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_StalledAgentTriage/Lane_Steward",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/session-coordinator",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_StalledAgentTriage",
      "label": "Merge steward",
      "scopeNote": "Receives the open PRs that lost their driver: which are green and ready, which are mid-merge, which must be re-driven from their PR head.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/stalled-agent-triage.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/integration-watcher",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Integration watcher",
      "title": "Integration watcher",
      "notation": "integration-watcher",
      "definition": "Watches the default branch and open branches for newly-landed work that an existing audit axis should be re-run over. Reports findings; does not author the fix.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/test-requester",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Test requester",
      "title": "Test requester",
      "notation": "test-requester",
      "definition": "Asks for a system under test to be certified against a named `test-plan/v1` (plan id and version). It may BE the system under test, or speak for it, and that is exactly why it carries no lane after the request: the requester never tests, checks or certifies, so the system never writes a verdict about itself (`untainted-verification`; the `test-sut-not-self-judged` criterion). Lane `Lane_Requester` in `test-plan-execution.bpmn`, bean `3o5b`.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Requester / system under test"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestPlanExecution/Lane_Requester"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestPlanExecution/Lane_Requester",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/test-requester",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TestPlanExecution",
      "label": "Requester / system under test",
      "scopeNote": "The system under test, or whoever speaks for it, asking for certification against plan P at a named version. Its only task is the request, and that is the design rather than an omission: the system under test never writes a verdict about itself, so after this lane it is the SUBJECT of the process and never a performer in it.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/tester",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Tester",
      "title": "Tester",
      "notation": "tester",
      "definition": "Runs a `test-plan/v1` against a system under test: resolves the plan, binds its test data (fixed and reviewed, or generated from template + params + seed, per `vm6m`), executes every case or skips it with a reason, and writes the `folio-test-run/v1` and the `test-report/v1`. UNTAINTED from the system under test — never the same actor — and it does not certify: the rollup it writes is what the certifier decides ON. Bean `3o5b`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SmeTestDataReview/Lane_Record",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestDataCuration/Lane_Tester",
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestPlanExecution/Lane_Tester"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_SmeTestDataReview/Lane_Record",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/tester",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_SmeTestDataReview",
      "label": "Tester",
      "scopeNote": "Records the SME's judgement as a validated `sme-case-verdict/1.0.0` node with attributable human `reviewer` identity and `reviewedAt` date, and updates the fixed data set's `review` status when passed.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/sme-test-data-review.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestDataCuration/Lane_Tester",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/tester",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TestDataCuration",
      "label": "Tester",
      "scopeNote": "Verifies that the curated fixed set or generated recipe self-identifies from its file content (`discriminateTestDataSet`) rather than from its directory path, verifies the canonical SHA-256 digest, and binds the `TestDataRef` into the `test-plan/v1` test case.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/test-data-curation.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestPlanExecution/Lane_Tester",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/tester",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TestPlanExecution",
      "label": "Tester",
      "scopeNote": "Runs the plan against the system: resolves it, binds its fixed or generated test data, executes every case or skips it with a reason, and writes the `folio-test-run/v1` and the `test-report/v1`. Untainted from the system under test — never the same actor — and it does not certify: what it writes is what the certifier decides on.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/untainted-checker",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Untainted checker",
      "title": "Untainted checker",
      "notation": "untainted-checker",
      "definition": "Re-executes a SAMPLE of a plan's cases from the plan and the data alone — never the tester's verdicts — and reports whether it agrees. It rules on nothing: agreement is a fact the certification table reads, not a verdict the checker writes (`untainted-verification` rule 3: one party doing both halves is not this check). Lane `Lane_Checker` in `test-plan-execution.bpmn`, bean `3o5b`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestPlanExecution/Lane_Checker"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestPlanExecution/Lane_Checker",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/untainted-checker",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TestPlanExecution",
      "label": "Untainted checker",
      "scopeNote": "A second party re-executing a sample of the cases from the plan and the data alone, never from the tester's verdicts. It rules on nothing: whether it agrees is a fact the certification table reads. One party doing both halves is not this check — it would compare a run with its own paraphrase of itself.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/certifier",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Certifier",
      "title": "Certifier",
      "notation": "certifier",
      "definition": "Takes the certification decision on ONE test report: applies the DMN the plan's `exitCriteria` names (computed from facts, never asserted) and records the decision as a judgement under the declared `attestations` graph, from which it is signed through `qa-report-signing.bpmn`. A specialisation of `stakeholder` — accountable sign-off — but NOT `judgementOnly`: the exit criteria are a table it applies, and only the decision on top of them is the judgement (owner ruling, 2026-10-01). Never the tester and never the system under test. Bean `3o5b`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "usage": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestPlanExecution/Lane_Certifier"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld#glossary-usage/Process_TestPlanExecution/Lane_Certifier",
      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/LaneUsage",
      "ofConcept": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/certifier",
      "inProcess": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/process/Process_TestPlanExecution",
      "label": "Certifier",
      "scopeNote": "The accountable party for the decision, a specialisation of the stakeholder. The gateway is computed from the plan's exit-criteria table; what the certifier adds, and what makes it a judgement, is recording the decision under their name. Never the tester and never the system under test.",
      "source": "cat-harness/sdlc/processes/test-plan-execution.bpmn"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/deep-researcher",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Deep researcher",
      "title": "Deep researcher",
      "notation": "deep-researcher",
      "definition": "Answers a question FROM a corpus already held, and is answerable for the answer. Distinct from `librarian`, which decides what to capture, and from `ingestion-agent`, which derives structure from what was captured: both produce the corpus, and this role consumes it. Added 2026-09-23 with the `doc-researcher` methodology, because the accountability it names — somebody who must stand behind a synthesis and its citations — belonged to no declared role. THE LANE IT BINDS IS DRAWN IN ANOTHER LAYER — the `Deep researcher` lane of `folio-assistant-core/processes/library/deep-document-research.bpmn`, which names this role with `<folio:role ref>`. It carried a `lanes[]` here for about an hour on 2026-09-23 before #1168 landed and inverted the relation: a lane names its role, and a role does not list its lanes, because a general node never names its users. The binding is therefore stated once, on the lane, and this role says nothing about where it is drawn.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/evidence-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Evidence agent",
      "title": "Evidence agent",
      "notation": "evidence-agent",
      "definition": "Retrieves and appraises external evidence for a guideline claim.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/onboarding-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Onboarding agent",
      "title": "Onboarding agent",
      "notation": "onboarding-agent",
      "definition": "The authoring agent acting before there is a folio: clarifying what the user means by \"create a folio\", scanning an existing repo, and scaffolding.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/authoring-committee",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Authoring Committee",
      "title": "Authoring Committee",
      "notation": "authoring-committee",
      "definition": "The people writing a document with its editor, while it is still a working draft: contributors who give feedback through the Contributor Feedback sheet, one change set per row, in their own Blue column. They recommend; an Editor decides, through the sheet's Ready columns. Added 2026-10-31 by the owner, so the drafting sheet names a process role rather than a job title, as the public-comment sheet names the Feedback Review Committee. The lane it binds is in folio-assistant-core/processes/content/contributor-feedback.bpmn and authoring-a-document.bpmn.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/fhir-modeller",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "FHIR modeller",
      "title": "FHIR modeller",
      "notation": "fhir-modeller",
      "definition": "Authors the L3 profiles, extensions and examples an IG is built from.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/ig-publisher-service",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "IG publisher + validator",
      "title": "IG publisher + validator",
      "notation": "ig-publisher-service",
      "definition": "The JVM services an IG build shells out to. External in behaviour, internal in configuration.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/iris-cdn-owner",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "IRIS CDN owner",
      "title": "IRIS CDN owner",
      "notation": "iris-cdn-owner",
      "definition": "A person: decides the export's scope, budget and storage target. Nothing downstream widens what the owner approved.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/iris-cdn-exporter",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "IRIS CDN Exporter",
      "title": "IRIS CDN Exporter",
      "notation": "iris-cdn-exporter",
      "definition": "The agent role. It plans, reviews and reports; it does not hold the signing key, and it never pushes to a WHO repository.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/cloudflare-r2-cdn",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Cloudflare R2 and CDN",
      "title": "Cloudflare R2 and CDN",
      "notation": "cloudflare-r2-cdn",
      "definition": "Object storage behind the CDN. Every object is named by its SHA-256 and served with an immutable cache policy; an object already present is never written again. Also serves did.json. A mechanical role, held to the contract its skills state.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/cloudflare-git",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Cloudflare git (Artifacts)",
      "title": "Cloudflare git (Artifacts)",
      "notation": "cloudflare-git",
      "definition": "A git repository hosted on Cloudflare Artifacts, not GitHub. Holds the release history: BagIt tag files, signatures, the cursor, checkpoints and run reports. A mechanical role: written to, deciding nothing.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/release-signer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Release signer",
      "title": "Release signer",
      "notation": "release-signer",
      "definition": "Holds the P-256 private key (GitHub environment secret IRIS_CDN_SIGNING_JWK) and signs each changed item manifest and the release tag manifest. A mechanical role.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/verifier",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "IRIS CDN verifier",
      "title": "IRIS CDN verifier",
      "notation": "verifier",
      "definition": "Anyone. Resolves the key from the did:web DID document, never from the package, and checks its x5c chain up to WHO's signing key. Cannot reach it: the verdict is unknown, not verified.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/lean-authoring-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Lean authoring agent",
      "title": "Lean authoring agent",
      "notation": "lean-authoring-agent",
      "definition": "Writes and repairs the Lean 4 formalization — translating narrative mathematics into declarations, keeping the build green, and curating what is staged for upstream.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/compute-authoring-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Compute authoring agent",
      "title": "Compute authoring agent",
      "notation": "compute-authoring-agent",
      "definition": "Writes and audits the computation scripts and simulators that produce witnessed values, and keeps the paper's numbers and its computations from drifting apart.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/proof-review-agent",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Proof review agent",
      "title": "Proof review agent",
      "notation": "proof-review-agent",
      "definition": "Reviews proofs — narrative and formal — for gaps, vacuity, redundancy and divergence between the two renderings of the same claim.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/lean-toolchain",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Lean toolchain",
      "title": "Lean toolchain",
      "notation": "lean-toolchain",
      "definition": "Elaborates and checks the formal half of a paper folio. Answers only what Lean can answer.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/l1-extraction-reviewer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "L1 extraction reviewer",
      "title": "L1 extraction reviewer",
      "notation": "l1-extraction-reviewer",
      "definition": "Signs, or rejects, the exclusions an L1 extraction proposes: each normative-looking sentence of a WHO publication that the curation says is not a recommendation, an implementation practice or a remark. Until a person acting in this role signs an exclusion, its sentence stays unaccounted and coverage stays below 100 %. Owner ruling 3b, 2026-10-12: exclusions are signed by this named role, never by the agent that proposed them. Inherits the harness's generic reviewer and performs exclusion sign-off in `classify-and-code-content.bpmn` (bean 4nfs).",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/health-worker",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Health worker",
      "title": "Health worker",
      "notation": "health-worker",
      "definition": "The generic DAK persona who delivers care at the point of care and records it on a device: completes the DAK's SDC forms and acts on its decision-support guidance (`questionnaire-data-capture.bpmn`, `act-on-decision-support.bpmn`). A DAK's own health-worker roles (a vaccinator, a community health worker) carry these skills or inherit this role. WHO's DAK personas call this a health worker; the role is a lane, never a person.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Health worker (WHO PHC digital transformation handbook)",
        "Healthcare Provider (SMART Base generic persona DAK.Persona.HealthcareProvider)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/point-of-care-system",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Point-of-care system",
      "title": "Point-of-care system",
      "notation": "point-of-care-system",
      "definition": "The app or EHR the health worker uses: renders the DAK's forms, extracts their resources, applies the DAK's decision tables (PlanDefinitions) and writes what the health worker accepted. Decides nothing clinical. A DAK's own systems (a CHW app, a clinic EHR) carry these skills or inherit this role.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Person-centred point of service system (PCPOSS, WHO PHC digital transformation handbook)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/holder",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Holder",
      "title": "Holder",
      "notation": "holder",
      "definition": "The person who holds a Personal Health Wallet, records consent, and presents verifiable health links and certificates. Specializes the ActorDefinition Holder (input/fsh/actors/actors.fsh).",
      "altLabel": [
        "Certificate Holder (person / Personal Health Wallet)",
        "Holder (person / Personal Health Wallet)",
        "VHL Holder (Patient / Personal Health Wallet)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/consent-recorder",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Consent Recorder",
      "title": "Consent Recorder",
      "notation": "consent-recorder",
      "definition": "The person or system that records a consent directive for the holder (IHE PCF Consent Recorder): the wallet itself, or a health worker on the holder's behalf.",
      "altLabel": [
        "PCF Consent Recorder (Wallet / VHL Sharer)",
        "PCF Consent Recorder (wallet or health worker)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/consent-registry",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Consent Registry",
      "title": "Consent Registry",
      "notation": "consent-registry",
      "definition": "Holds consent directives and answers IHE PCF [ITI-108] Access Consent. Specializes the ActorDefinition ConsentRegistry (input/fsh/actors/actors.fsh).",
      "altLabel": [
        "PCF Consent Registry"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/vhl-sharer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "VHL Sharer",
      "title": "VHL Sharer",
      "notation": "vhl-sharer",
      "definition": "Holds the health information, generates verifiable health links, and enforces consent when a link is redeemed. Specializes the ActorDefinition Issuer (input/fsh/actors/actors.fsh).",
      "altLabel": [
        "VHL Sharer (enforcement and decision point)",
        "VHL Sharer (grouped with PCF Consent Recorder)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/document-source",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Document Source",
      "title": "Document Source",
      "notation": "document-source",
      "definition": "The system that assembles a document about the holder before it is signed: the VHL Sharer when a document is shared, the Certificate Issuance Service when a certificate is issued. Adds the consent directives to it (process M).",
      "altLabel": [
        "Document source (VHL Sharer or Certificate Issuance Service)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/vhl-receiver",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "VHL Receiver",
      "title": "VHL Receiver",
      "notation": "vhl-receiver",
      "definition": "Receives a verifiable health link, checks its signature against the trust list, and retrieves the information. Specializes the ActorDefinition Receiver (input/fsh/actors/actors.fsh).",
      "altLabel": [
        "VHL Receiver (Verifier / Relying Party)",
        "VHL Receiver (receiving organisation or application)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/trust-anchor",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Trust Anchor",
      "title": "Trust Anchor",
      "notation": "trust-anchor",
      "definition": "Publishes the trust list of keys that participants use to check signatures. GDHCN is one possible anchor among others. Specializes the ActorDefinition TrustNetworkAnchor (input/fsh/actors/actors.fsh).",
      "altLabel": [
        "Trust Anchor (GDHCN or another accepted anchor)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/certificate-issuer",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Certificate Issuer",
      "title": "Certificate Issuer",
      "notation": "certificate-issuer",
      "definition": "A health worker or issuing system that issues a verifiable digital health certificate. Specializes the ActorDefinition Issuer (input/fsh/actors/actors.fsh).",
      "altLabel": [
        "Certificate Issuer (health worker or issuing system)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/certificate-verifier",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Verifier",
      "title": "Verifier",
      "notation": "certificate-verifier",
      "definition": "Checks a certificate and its status, with or without a status checking application. Specializes the ActorDefinition Receiver (input/fsh/actors/actors.fsh).",
      "altLabel": [
        "Verifier (with or without a status checking application)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/data-provider-administrator",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Data Provider Administrator",
      "title": "Data Provider Administrator",
      "notation": "data-provider-administrator",
      "definition": "The person at a data provider who registers clients under a data sharing agreement.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Data Provider Administrator (person)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/data-recipient-system",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Data Recipient System",
      "title": "Data Recipient System",
      "notation": "data-recipient-system",
      "definition": "A server that accesses data under a data sharing agreement (OAuth client) and performs the agreement's duties.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Data Recipient (duty performer)",
        "Data Recipient System (OAuth client)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/provider-authorization-server",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Provider Authorization Server",
      "title": "Provider Authorization Server",
      "notation": "provider-authorization-server",
      "definition": "Registers clients and decides access under a data sharing agreement (policy decision and enforcement).",
      "altLabel": [
        "Policy Decision Point (permits())",
        "Provider Authorization Server (administrator + decision point)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/role/auditor",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Auditor",
      "title": "Auditor",
      "notation": "auditor",
      "definition": "The person who reviews audit and provenance records under a data sharing agreement.",
      "altLabel": [
        "Auditor (person)"
      ],
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/archimate",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Archimate",
      "title": "Archimate",
      "notation": "kind/archimate",
      "definition": "ArchiMate models a layer holds, as Archi `.archimate` files (plain XML or Archi's zipped archive), named by `cat-archimate.config.json` (cat-harness's `archimate` subgraph). Every view, element and relationship in a model is a node of its own: a page and an IRI, keyed by Archi's own id, and every view is drawn as SVG from the model's diagram.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/attestations",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Attestations",
      "title": "Attestations",
      "notation": "kind/attestations",
      "definition": "QA attestations — the judgements a QA family carries across runs (pair attestations, voice reviews, agent and human verdicts, bibliography verifications and human reviews), one `qa-attestations/v1` file per subject, mirroring the derived family's tree. Kept on main where deleting derived results cannot reach them; each entry pins the hash it attested, so a stale one is detectable.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/auto-docs",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Auto docs",
      "title": "Auto docs",
      "notation": "kind/auto-docs",
      "definition": "Derived indexes over the other graphs — one page per auto-doc TYPE crossed with each SUB-GRAPH that type reaches. A sub-graph of `docs`, written by `scripts/gen-auto-docs.ts` and never by hand. Distinct from `docs` itself by the one question that settles the layer: a docs page is re-authored, an index is regenerated.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/basic-cdn-site",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Basic CDN site",
      "title": "Basic CDN site",
      "notation": "kind/basic-cdn-site",
      "definition": "A published static site on a CDN that serves files by path only (GitHub Pages): its routes, the commit it was built from, and its files as archive entries. Built from the renderable graphs its directory names, and deployed by the Tool its storage names.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/bean-defs",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Work items",
      "title": "Work items",
      "notation": "kind/bean-defs",
      "definition": "Work items — one Markdown file each, in the layout the `beans` CLI reads, carrying `$schema: bean/1.0.0` in its front matter. Authored and edited by people and agents.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/bean-notes",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Bean notes",
      "title": "Bean notes",
      "notation": "kind/bean-notes",
      "definition": "Bean notes — one Markdown file per pull request per bean, `$schema: folio-bean-note/v1` in its front matter, named `<bean>--<date>--<branch>.md` so two pull requests never write one path. Indexed by a generated README.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/beans",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Plans and work",
      "title": "Plans and work",
      "notation": "kind/beans",
      "definition": "The work plan — what is being worked on, and where each running BPMN instance got to. Its inner directories are declared by `beans/beans.json`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld",
      "hiddenLabel": [
        "Work plan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/binary-release",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Binary releases",
      "title": "Binary releases",
      "notation": "kind/binary-release",
      "definition": "Published binary releases -- one `folio-binary-release/v1` document per release, carrying its id, version and origin, and for each asset the size, the sha256 where one is known, where it is fetched from, and what became of it. Never the bytes: the schema is strict throughout, and a file a deploy phase deleted must still say where to get it back and why it went.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/block-kinds",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Block kinds",
      "title": "Block kinds",
      "notation": "kind/block-kinds",
      "definition": "The block kinds a harness's adapter owns, one node per kind carrying its label prefix, RDF types, profile and builder. Discovered across the instances; no module lists them.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/board-positions",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Board positions",
      "title": "Board positions",
      "notation": "kind/board-positions",
      "definition": "Where each note sits on each board — `board-positions.json`, keyed by board then by note id, in board units. The layout layer, which points at notes and is never pointed back at. Schema: `schemas/ui/board-positions.ts`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/boards",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Boards",
      "title": "Boards",
      "notation": "kind/boards",
      "definition": "Boards — one JSON file each, carrying `\"$schema\": \"folio-board/v1\"`. A board is a diagram OF a folio: it declares what it shows, and a folio with no board is complete. Schema: `schemas/ui/board.ts`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/building-blocks",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Building blocks",
      "title": "Building blocks",
      "notation": "kind/building-blocks",
      "definition": "Building-block catalogues -- layers and blocks (tools, systems, standards, trust networks) with their jurisdiction and what each is, the targets of a journey step's `uses` edges.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/business-processes",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Business processes",
      "title": "Business processes",
      "notation": "kind/business-processes",
      "definition": "BPMN that describes work as content (a guideline's business processes), drawn by the processes viewer and never run.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/cache",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "CI caches",
      "title": "CI caches",
      "notation": "kind/cache",
      "definition": "CI caches -- one `cache/1.0.0` node per cache a layer declares: key recipe, trust class, location, producer, consumers, save policy, verify and budget. Never the entries; the stored key, size and hit rate come from the daily cache report, so staleness is computed, never claimed.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/cat-harness",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Harness graph",
      "title": "Harness graph",
      "notation": "kind/cat-harness",
      "definition": "A Subgraph holding a Harness's own parts, such as Skills, Processes and Roles, where one directory holds more than one of them.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/cdn-site",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "CDN site",
      "title": "CDN site",
      "notation": "kind/cdn-site",
      "definition": "A published site on a CDN that also controls media types, redirects and headers: a `basic-cdn-site` plus those three. No instance declares one yet.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/code",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Code",
      "title": "Code",
      "notation": "kind/code",
      "definition": "Source code -- the modules, scripts and entry points an instance holds. Declared so that code is scannable at all: an undeclared file is one no checker has a reason to look at. Being declared here says nothing about whether a Tool node claims it, which is a separate question and a separate axis.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/code-list",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Code lists",
      "title": "Code lists",
      "notation": "kind/code-list",
      "definition": "Closed sets of codes — adjudication answers, the namespaces this project mints — one file per list, every code carrying its definition and source, published as SKOS.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/content-adapters",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Content adapters",
      "title": "Content adapters",
      "notation": "kind/content-adapters",
      "definition": "The block vocabularies a harness owns, one node per vocabulary carrying its companion roles and whether the platform's code types it. Discovered across the instances; no module lists them.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/device-screen",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Device screens",
      "title": "Device screens",
      "notation": "kind/device-screen",
      "definition": "Device screens -- what one person sees on one device at a journey step, as typed data-only blocks (QR code, passcode, verdict, record list, consent), drawn as a device mock.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/doc-group",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Doc group",
      "title": "Doc group",
      "notation": "kind/doc-group",
      "definition": "A named group of the documentation's own pages — one folder, one heading in the Pages list. A sub-graph of `docs`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/docs",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Docs",
      "title": "Docs",
      "notation": "kind/docs",
      "definition": "Documentation ABOUT the knowledge graph — how the harness works, what its directories hold, how a process runs. Rendered by the plain just-the-docs pipeline. Distinct from `folio`, which is content an author CREATES using the graph; the difference is the SUBJECT, not the format. An L1 library's catalogue is `library/`; a note about it is a `folio`; the page explaining how ingestion works is `docs`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/document-kinds",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Document kinds",
      "title": "Document kinds",
      "notation": "kind/document-kinds",
      "definition": "Document kinds — named structures of sections (fixed or semi-fixed) that a document authored with a harness follows, one `document-kind/1.0.0` JSON each, plus computed `document-kind-coverage/1.0.0` reports of how a subject realises one. Every kind and section names its sources; `computedFrom` names the declared graphs a section derives from.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/external-schema",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "External schemas",
      "title": "External schemas",
      "notation": "kind/external-schema",
      "definition": "The specifications this instance depends on — one record per specification, pinning the EDITION in use, with the operative terms derived from the corpus rather than hand-listed; and, beside a record, the pinned edition's own codes where something resolves against them.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/folio",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Folio",
      "title": "Folio",
      "notation": "kind/folio",
      "definition": "Authored content, rendered to a website by the just-the-docs pipeline.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/fsh-guts",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "FSH guts",
      "title": "FSH guts",
      "notation": "kind/fsh-guts",
      "definition": "Deprecated and throwaway structured content — kept, addressable and exported, and deliberately absent from the rendered site. The destination for anything that would otherwise be deleted, and for SDLC churn that must not reach the folio's readers.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/health",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Health",
      "title": "Health",
      "notation": "kind/health",
      "definition": "Repository health reports — one `health-report/v1` document per sweep, carrying every check's three-state verdict, the thresholds it applied and the basis each threshold was chosen on. Generated by `test/health/run.ts`; never hand-edited.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/interaction",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Interaction",
      "title": "Interaction",
      "notation": "kind/interaction",
      "definition": "How a person wants to be asked — read at session start, never written by a process.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/issue-marks",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Issue marks",
      "title": "Issue marks",
      "notation": "kind/issue-marks",
      "definition": "How far an agent has read an issue — the comment id and the edit time it accounted for.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/library",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Library",
      "title": "Library",
      "notation": "kind/library",
      "definition": "L1 source content — one `<bib-slug>/` per ingested document, holding `sections/*.md`, `structure.json` and, where the source was scanned, `ocr/page-NNN.txt`. Every knowledge-graph reference to a source resolves through here, never to a loose path or a bare URL.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/memory",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Memory",
      "title": "Memory",
      "notation": "kind/memory",
      "definition": "Durable facts an agent carries between sessions. Read during a process, never written by one.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/merge-queue",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Merge queue",
      "title": "Merge queue",
      "notation": "kind/merge-queue",
      "definition": "A merge steward's DECISIONS about an open pull request — priority, rank or override with its reason, a hold with its expiry, the train it joined, an ejection with its evidence. Never a fact GitHub owns: CI, mergeability, labels and the head SHA are read live and refused by name here.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/merge-reviews",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Merge reviews",
      "title": "Merge reviews",
      "notation": "kind/merge-reviews",
      "definition": "The adversarial review verdict on a pull request's head, one file per head sha.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/methodology",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Methodologies",
      "title": "Methodologies",
      "notation": "kind/methodology",
      "definition": "Judgement methodologies, adopted whole and kept independent — parallel ways to reach a decision, selected by context.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/notes",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Notes",
      "title": "Notes",
      "notation": "kind/notes",
      "definition": "A folio's derivation notes, scoping docs and ledgers as declared context, not rendered content.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/openapi",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Openapi",
      "title": "Openapi",
      "notation": "kind/openapi",
      "definition": "OpenAPI 3 documents a layer holds, each verbatim beside a provenance node naming the repository, path and commit it was ingested from (cat-harness's `openapi` subgraph). Every operation in a document is a node of its own: a page and an IRI under the layer's docs.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/pipeline-plugins",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Pipeline plugins",
      "title": "Pipeline plugins",
      "notation": "kind/pipeline-plugins",
      "definition": "The generic pipeline slots a harness fills, one node per slot naming the table of implementations; registered for a folio through its dependency tree.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/policies",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Policies",
      "title": "Policies",
      "notation": "kind/policies",
      "definition": "W3C ODRL 2.2 policies: which Actor may do which action, scoped by Process, Task and Role constraints. Actions are the folio profile in skills/permissions/permissions.json.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/proposals",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Proposals",
      "title": "Proposals",
      "notation": "kind/proposals",
      "definition": "Proposals for the harness's own features — initial analysis, MVP, options — argued before anything is agreed. A sub-graph of `docs`. When the feature ships, its proposal is MOVED to `requirements` and filed against the `Requirement` schema.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/qa",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "QA",
      "title": "QA",
      "notation": "kind/qa",
      "definition": "QA verdicts and their projections — kg-qa audits, block and translation QA, qa-witness documents for the docs site, the viewer-navbar audit, result roll-ups and test runs; every `$schema` family is named in `nodeSchemas`, which is the list — a count here would be a second one, and it was already wrong by one before `viewer-nav-qa/v1` was added. Generated; never hand-edited.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/qa-checkers",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "QA checkers",
      "title": "QA checkers",
      "notation": "kind/qa-checkers",
      "definition": "The QA checkers a harness provides, one node per criterion naming the table that holds the code; registered for a folio through its dependency tree.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/qa-report",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "QA reports",
      "title": "QA reports",
      "notation": "kind/qa-report",
      "definition": "QA reports -- one `qa-report/v1` document per tool run, carrying the tool's own successes, warnings and errors, the files it processed, the files it EXPECTED and the ones that were missing, plus the provenance and toolchain versions upstream records nowhere. Generated by the run; never hand-edited.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/requirements",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Requirements",
      "title": "Requirements",
      "notation": "kind/requirements",
      "definition": "What the harness promises, one document per shipped feature, each carrying a `Requirement` in its front matter. A sub-graph of `docs`. Test runs point at these statements by `req:<slug>#<key>`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/session-state",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Session state",
      "title": "Session state",
      "notation": "kind/session-state",
      "definition": "A session's context — the acting actor, the instances it has open, and what it waits on.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/session-survey",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Session surveys",
      "title": "Session surveys",
      "notation": "kind/session-survey",
      "definition": "Published surveys of a commit window — one JSON file each, carrying `\"$schema\": \"folio-session-survey/v1\"` and the window's two edge commits, so a later session can compute what it is NOT covered for instead of re-deriving the whole range (bean `6ptx`).",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/sme-case-verdict",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "SME case/verdict pairs",
      "title": "SME case/verdict pairs",
      "notation": "kind/sme-case-verdict",
      "definition": "SME review case/verdict pairs — one `sme-case-verdict/1.0.0` document per reviewed decision-support worked case or indicator-definition cohort, recording attributable human SME identity and review date (bean `vljz`).",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/software-library",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Software libraries",
      "title": "Software libraries",
      "notation": "kind/software-library",
      "definition": "Outside libraries a layer imports or vendors -- one generated `software-library` node per library per layer, with the version and sha512 its `bun.lock` pins, its SPDX licence, its range, whether it is a dev dependency, the files that import it and the shim that types it. Shares its core with `tool-release`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/subscribed-harnesses",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Subscribed harness state",
      "title": "Subscribed harness state",
      "notation": "kind/subscribed-harnesses",
      "definition": "The state directories of each harness instantiated from a KG subscription, one home per subscription and harness, kept apart from the read-only snapshots.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/substrate-snapshot",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Substrate snapshots",
      "title": "Substrate snapshots",
      "notation": "kind/substrate-snapshot",
      "definition": "The root declaration of each Knowledge Graph this instance subscribes to, cached byte for byte at the pinned commit with its fixity, and what the substrate judgement found in it; and each chosen subgraph or asset materialised from it, with its fixity, provenance and gate answers.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/sweep-marks",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Sweep marks",
      "title": "Sweep marks",
      "notation": "kind/sweep-marks",
      "definition": "When a sweep step last ran — one JSON per check, carrying `\"$schema\": \"folio-sweep-mark/v1\"`, so a skipped `check:session-staleness` is visible after the terminal scrolls (bean `rq8s`).",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/swimlane-glossary",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Swimlane glossary",
      "title": "Swimlane glossary",
      "notation": "kind/swimlane-glossary",
      "definition": "A Subgraph recording every term a Knowledge Graph's Processes have ever named, and when each stopped being used, so a retired term is never silently reused.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/test-data-fixed",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Fixed test data sets",
      "title": "Fixed test data sets",
      "notation": "kind/test-data-fixed",
      "definition": "Fixed test data sets — one `test-data-fixed/1.0.0` document per curated set (`kind: \"fixed\"`), living in its own declared directory separate from `test-data-generated` and self-identifying from the file content rather than the path (bean `vm6m`).",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/test-data-generated",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Generated test data recipes",
      "title": "Generated test data recipes",
      "notation": "kind/test-data-generated",
      "definition": "Generated test data recipes — one `test-data-generated/1.0.0` document per recipe (`kind: \"generated\"`, `template`, `params`, `seed`, `specialisation`, `sha256`), never stored materialised, living in a declared directory separate from `test-data-fixed` (bean `vm6m`).",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/test-plan",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Test plan",
      "title": "Test plan",
      "notation": "kind/test-plan",
      "definition": "Test plans -- one `test-plan/v1` document per plan, in the FHIR R5 TestPlan shape: the system-under-test kind and version range, the `req:` requirements it is evidence for, test cases whose assertions are criterion ids, fixed (reviewed) or generated (template + params + seed) test data, and the certification rule as a DMN reference.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/test-report",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Test report",
      "title": "Test report",
      "notation": "kind/test-report",
      "definition": "Test reports -- one `test-report/v1` document per run of a plan against a system under test: per-case verdicts in the block-qa entry shape, a rollup for that ONE plan that may not disagree with its cases, and never a total across plans. `running` is never a pass, and the system under test never writes its own verdict. Generated by the run.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/themes",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Themes",
      "title": "Themes",
      "notation": "kind/themes",
      "definition": "Themes derived from an instance's own sources — one Theme node each, carrying `kind: sticky | webpage | publication`. The palette vocabulary is shared across every kind and only the geometry varies; every value cites where it was measured.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/todo-feedback",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Todo feedback",
      "title": "Todo feedback",
      "notation": "kind/todo-feedback",
      "definition": "Feedback items — todos raised against a specific block, carrying the submitter's identity. Read by the `todo-review` skill.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/todo-items",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Todo items",
      "title": "Todo items",
      "notation": "kind/todo-items",
      "definition": "Todo nodes — one file each, carrying `\"$schema\": \"todo/1.0.0\"`. Authored by people and by agents on their behalf.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/todos",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Todos",
      "title": "Todos",
      "notation": "kind/todos",
      "definition": "Human actors' outstanding work — content, owned by the folio, tagged by role, process, task and identity. Its inner directories are declared by `todos/todos.json`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/tool-release",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Tool releases",
      "title": "Tool releases",
      "notation": "kind/tool-release",
      "definition": "External tool releases -- one `folio-tool-release/v1` document per tool at one version, with its sha256, its source (an OCI image only by digest), its SPDX licence, how to run it, and the runtimes that release needs, injected rather than inherited -- and the named `folio-tool-profile/v1` sets a run selects. A profile never names a runtime.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/tools",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Tools",
      "title": "Tools",
      "notation": "kind/tools",
      "definition": "Tool definitions — themselves nodes in the KG, per the repo taxonomy.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/translation-sources",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Translation sources",
      "title": "Translation sources",
      "notation": "kind/translation-sources",
      "definition": "POT templates, PO catalogues and their `TranslationNode` manifests, one directory per target locale. The INPUT to injection; the rendered output is ordinary content that declares its own `lang`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/typologies",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Graph typologies",
      "title": "Graph typologies",
      "notation": "kind/typologies",
      "definition": "The graph typologies a harness declares it owns, one node per kind, so no central registry names another harness's subgraph types. Loaded across the instances on first use.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/uml",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "UML",
      "title": "UML",
      "notation": "kind/uml",
      "definition": "UML class diagrams of each named sub-graph a harness declares, derived from the node schemas its graph typologies register — PlantUML and Mermaid from one model.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/uploads",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Uploads",
      "title": "Uploads",
      "notation": "kind/uploads",
      "definition": "The incoming queue — raw files as dropped, before ingestion. NOT L1, and not greppable as corpus: a document here reads as absent to every consumer.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/user-scenario",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "User scenarios",
      "title": "User scenarios",
      "notation": "kind/user-scenario",
      "definition": "User scenarios as journey maps -- one file per journey: ordered steps, per actor what they do and feel, pain points, enablers, the record's trust state, and edges to user stories, BPMN tasks, requirements, FHIR examples, the building blocks each step uses and its DAK assets; a DAK user scenario, composed of other journeys in order.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/validators",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Validators",
      "title": "Validators",
      "notation": "kind/validators",
      "definition": "The validators a harness's code provides, one node each naming the graph typology and $schema family it checks and the Zod export that checks it, joined onto the kinds on first use.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/vocab-mapping",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Vocab mapping",
      "title": "Vocab mapping",
      "notation": "kind/vocab-mapping",
      "definition": "Vocabulary mappings — which source field becomes which target predicate, with its stated relationship, one ConceptMap-shaped table per source and target; representable from and producible as a FHIR ConceptMap.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/voice-vendors",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Voice vendors",
      "title": "Voice vendors",
      "notation": "kind/voice-vendors",
      "definition": "Vendor voice profiles — a base voice specialised for one agent vendor, `folio-voice/v1` with `extends` naming the base. A sub-graph of `voices`, declared from within by `voices.json`, each vendor declared by `vendors.json`.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/voices",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Voices",
      "title": "Voices",
      "notation": "kind/voices",
      "definition": "Editorial voice profiles — one JSON each, carrying `\"$schema\": \"folio-voice/v1\"`. Every rule cites the ingested source or KG node it was derived from. Opt-in per folio.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/waiver",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Waivers",
      "title": "Waivers",
      "notation": "kind/waiver",
      "definition": "Confirmations a person granted in advance — each naming one gate, scoped to a session or a process run, each expiring.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/web-app",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Web apps",
      "title": "Web apps",
      "notation": "kind/web-app",
      "definition": "A web app held as source and published as its own chrome-less page, built at publish by the web-app-build Tool and loaded only when a reader opens its route.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/workflow-state",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Workflow state",
      "title": "Workflow state",
      "notation": "kind/workflow-state",
      "definition": "Running BPMN instances — one JSON file each, carrying `\"$schema\": \"folio-workflow-instance/v1\"`. Owned by the interpreter, never hand-edited.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/graphTypology/workshop",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "prefLabel": "Workshops",
      "title": "Workshops",
      "notation": "kind/workshop",
      "definition": "Workshops over journeys -- modules, learning objectives, questions for the room per journey step, reference tables, printable sheets, job aids and readings.",
      "inScheme": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/branches/repin-train-20261113-1024/cat-harness/cat-harness-glossary.jsonld"
    },
    {
